$schema: https://usm.dev/schema/v1.json
$id: usm/cli-color-output
$type: feature
$version: 1
$last_updated: "2026-08-26"
summary: >-
  Comprehensive CLI polish for the USM CLI — colorized status output, animated spinners with elapsed
  time for long operations, progress bars for batch file operations, tree-view rendering of file
  lists, an ASCII art USM banner on no-args/help, did-you-mean suggestions for typos, a non-blocking
  update-notifier hint, and --quiet/--verbose verbosity flags. Uses battle-tested libraries
  (picocolors, ora, cli-progress, treeify, update-notifier) pinned to CJS-compatible versions. All
  honor NO_COLOR and non-TTY (pipes/CI) by emitting plain text automatically.
$system: usm/system
$service: usm/cli
intent: >-
  The CLI ships plain monochrome text with no progress feedback, flat file lists, no typo help, and
  no update awareness — it feels dated and is hard to scan during long operations. A comprehensive
  polish layer using battle-tested CLI libraries adds colorized status (green ✓, red ✗, yellow ⚠,
  cyan →, dim secondary), animated spinners with elapsed time for async work, progress bars for
  batch operations, tree-view file lists, an ASCII brand banner, did-you-mean suggestions, a
  non-blocking update notifier, and --quiet/--verbose flags. Every layer degrades gracefully to
  plain text in non-TTY/CI/NO_COLOR environments.
status: built
decisions:
  - id: use-deps-not-inline
    decision: Use battle-tested CLI libraries, not hand-rolled inline helpers
    rationale: >-
      Libraries like picocolors, ora, cli-progress, and update-notifier are tiny, battle-tested by
      millions of downloads, and handle edge cases (Windows terminals, truecolor detection, spinner
      cleanup) that inline code would miss. Less code to maintain, better UX, and they auto-install
      via npm with no user action needed.
    alternatives:
      - option: Strictly zero new deps (all inline)
        rejected_because: More code to maintain, misses edge cases, reinvents wheels
    consequences: >-
      Adds ~5 small runtime dependencies to package.json, all pinned to CJS-compatible versions
      (ora@5, cli-progress@3, update-notifier@5 — newer majors are ESM-only and incompatible with
      the CJS package).
    status: accepted
  - id: respect-no-color
    decision: Honor NO_COLOR env var and non-TTY stdout/stderr by emitting plain text
    rationale: >-
      Standard CLI convention (https://no-color.org) and CI hygiene. Piped/redirected output must
      stay plain so logs and grep work; colored escape codes in CI logs are noise. picocolors
      respects NO_COLOR natively; ora disables spinner in non-TTY.
    consequences: >-
      Color helpers short-circuit when process.stdout.isTTY is false or NO_COLOR is set.
      Spinner/progress bars suppressed in non-TTY.
    status: accepted
  - id: palette
    decision: green=✓, red=✗, yellow=⚠, cyan=→/info, dim=secondary values
    rationale: >-
      Conventional semantic mapping that reads correctly in both light and dark terminals. Dim for
      file paths and counts keeps the primary message in foreground.
    consequences: Single palette in src/cli/colors.ts applied consistently
    status: accepted
  - id: cjs-pin-versions
    decision: Pin dependency versions to CJS-compatible majors
    rationale: >-
      The package is CommonJS (no type field = module). Newer majors of ora (v6+) and
      update-notifier (v7+) are ESM-only and would break the CJS build. Pin to the last
      CJS-compatible major.
    consequences: >-
      package.json dependencies list exact major versions: picocolors (^1), ora (^5), cli-progress
      (^3), treeify (^0.1), update-notifier (^5).
    status: accepted
flows:
  - id: color-output
    name: Colored status output across all commands
    description: >-
      Every success/error/warning/skip/info line uses color helpers. Symbols are colored (green ✓,
      red ✗, yellow ⚠, dim ⊘, cyan →). File paths and counts dimmed.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: import
        target: color helpers from src/cli/colors.ts (picocolors wrapper)
      - id: s2
        action: replace
        target: console.log with success symbol → success() helper
      - id: s3
        action: replace
        target: console.error with fail symbol → error() helper
      - id: s4
        action: replace
        target: console.warn with warn symbol → warning() helper
  - id: spinner-flow
    name: Spinner during long operations
    description: >-
      scan, enrich, generate show a spinner with elapsed seconds while work is in progress. Spinner
      clears on completion and is replaced by the result line.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: start
        target: ora spinner before async work begins
      - id: s2
        action: tick
        target: spinner updates with next frame automatically
      - id: s3
        action: stop
        target: spinner.succeed() or spinner.fail() with colored result
      - id: s4
        action: fallback
        target: non-TTY shows plain log line (ora auto-disables)
  - id: progress-flow
    name: Progress bar for batch operations
    description: >-
      generate writing N files and scan detecting N services show an inline progress bar that
      updates without scrolling.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: init
        target: cli-progress single bar with total count
      - id: s2
        action: update
        target: bar.increment() after each file written
      - id: s3
        action: complete
        target: bar.stop(), newline, summary line
      - id: s4
        action: fallback
        target: non-TTY logs count only (bar auto-disabled)
  - id: tree-flow
    name: Tree view for file lists
    description: >-
      Files written/skipped lists render as a tree with connectors mirroring .usm/ structure via
      treeify.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: collect
        target: file paths from result
      - id: s2
        action: build
        target: nested object from path segments
      - id: s3
        action: render
        target: treeify.asTree() with dimmed paths via picocolors
      - id: s4
        action: fallback
        target: non-TTY flat list
  - id: banner-flow
    name: ASCII banner on no-args/help
    description: usm with no args shows an ASCII USM banner then the help text.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: detect
        target: no args or --help flag
      - id: s2
        action: render
        target: ASCII banner constant from banner.ts
      - id: s3
        action: follow
        target: with help text and command list
  - id: did-you-mean-flow
    name: Did you mean suggestions for typos
    description: >-
      Unknown command triggers a did-you-mean suggestion. Commander has built-in suggestion support
      — just needs enabling.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: detect
        target: unknown command
      - id: s2
        action: configure
        target: program.showSuggestionAfterError = true
      - id: s3
        action: render
        target: Commander emits did-you-mean closest match
  - id: update-flow
    name: Update notifier hint
    description: >-
      Non-blocking check of npm registry for newer @smithgray/usm. Cached 24h. One-line hint if
      newer exists.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: init
        target: update-notifier with 24h check interval
      - id: s2
        action: notify
        target: updateNotifier.notify() renders one-line hint in TTY
      - id: s3
        action: fallback
        target: suppressed in non-TTY automatically
  - id: verbosity-flow
    name: Verbosity flags
    description: Global --quiet and --verbose flags control output level across all commands.
    steps:
      - id: s1
        action: parse
        target: "--quiet / --verbose global options via Commander"
      - id: s2
        action: route
        target: "--quiet routes to errors and final summary only"
      - id: s3
        action: route
        target: "--verbose routes to timestamps, full paths, debug"
      - id: s4
        action: default
        target: current output level
contracts:
  - id: symbols-colored
    description: Status symbols are colored in TTY output
    must_have:
      - ✓ green
      - ✗ red
      - ⚠ yellow
      - ⊘ dim/yellow
      - → cyan
  - id: no-color-respected
    description: NO_COLOR env var disables all color
    must_have:
      - NO_COLOR set → output is plain text
      - NO_COLOR unset → colors active in TTY
  - id: non-tty-plain
    description: Piped/redirected output is plain text
    must_have:
      - stdout not a TTY → no ANSI codes
      - stderr not a TTY → no ANSI codes
      - spinner suppressed in non-TTY
      - progress bar suppressed in non-TTY
      - output remains grep-friendly
  - id: palette-consistent
    description: Color semantics are consistent across all commands
    must_have:
      - success states green across init/scan/validate/generate/enrich/etc
      - error states red across all commands
      - warning states yellow across all commands
      - file paths and counts dim across all commands
  - id: deps-cjs-compatible
    description: All new dependencies are CJS-compatible
    must_have:
      - picocolors ^1 (CJS)
      - ora ^5 (last CJS major; v6+ is ESM)
      - cli-progress ^3 (CJS)
      - treeify ^0.1 (CJS)
      - update-notifier ^5 (last CJS major; v7+ is ESM)
      - package.json remains CommonJS (no module type field)
  - id: spinner-long-ops
    description: Animated spinner during async operations
    must_have:
      - scan, enrich, generate show spinner with elapsed context
      - spinner clears and is replaced by result line on completion
      - spinner suppressed in non-TTY (plain log fallback)
  - id: progress-batch
    description: Progress bar for batch file operations
    must_have:
      - generate writing N files shows progress bar with current/total
      - scan detecting services shows count progress
      - bar hidden in non-TTY
  - id: tree-file-lists
    description: File lists rendered as tree view
    must_have:
      - Files written/skipped lists use tree connectors
      - nested .usm/ structure shown hierarchically
      - flat fallback in non-TTY
  - id: ascii-banner
    description: ASCII art USM banner on no-args/help
    must_have:
      - usm with no args shows ASCII USM banner then help
      - banner suppressed in non-TTY
  - id: did-you-mean
    description: Suggestions for unknown commands
    must_have:
      - usm scaan suggests scan via did-you-mean
      - suggestion shown via Commander built-in
  - id: update-notifier
    description: One-line hint when a newer @smithgray/usm is published
    must_have:
      - checks npm registry in background, non-blocking
      - cached with 24h interval
      - hint only shown if newer version exists and in TTY
  - id: verbosity-flags
    description: "--quiet and --verbose flags across commands"
    must_have:
      - "--quiet shows only errors and final summary"
      - default shows current output level
      - "--verbose shows timestamps, full paths, debug info"
tests:
  - id: tty-colored
    setup:
      tty: true
      no_color_unset: true
    expect:
      - assertion: success lines contain green ANSI codes
      - assertion: error lines contain red ANSI codes
  - id: no-color-plain
    setup:
      env:
        NO_COLOR: "1"
    expect:
      - assertion: no ANSI escape codes in output
      - assertion: symbols still present as plain characters
  - id: piped-plain
    setup:
      stdout_not_tty: true
    expect:
      - assertion: no ANSI escape codes in piped output
      - assertion: no spinner animation in piped output
      - assertion: no progress bar in piped output
  - id: spinner-during-async
    setup:
      tty: true
      long_op: true
    expect:
      - assertion: spinner frames appear while work in progress
      - assertion: spinner cleared on completion
  - id: progress-bar-batch
    setup:
      tty: true
      batch_op: true
    expect:
      - assertion: bar appears with current/total
      - assertion: bar at 100% on completion
  - id: tree-file-list
    setup:
      tty: true
      generate_run: true
    expect:
      - assertion: file list uses tree connectors
      - assertion: .usm structure shown hierarchically
  - id: ascii-banner
    setup:
      no_args: true
    expect:
      - assertion: ASCII USM banner rendered
      - assertion: help text follows banner
  - id: did-you-mean
    setup:
      command: scaan
    expect:
      - assertion: did-you-mean scan suggestion shown
  - id: update-notifier
    setup:
      newer_version_available: true
    expect:
      - assertion: one-line Update available hint in TTY
      - assertion: hint suppressed in non-TTY
  - id: verbosity-quiet
    setup:
      flag: "--quiet"
    expect:
      - assertion: only errors and final summary shown
      - assertion: success lines suppressed
  - id: verbosity-verbose
    setup:
      flag: "--verbose"
    expect:
      - assertion: timestamps present
      - assertion: full paths shown
  - id: all-commands-covered
    setup:
      review: true
    expect:
      - assertion: >-
          init, scan, validate, generate, enrich, scaffold, info, check, query, import, docs, mcp
          all use color/spinner/verbosity helpers
implementation:
  primary: src/cli/index.ts
  test_code: ""
  test_code_status: none
see_also:
  - usm/cli
